# Code Style and Standards

## Flutter/Dart Standards
- Follow the [official Flutter style guide](mdc:https:/dart.dev/guides/language/effective-dart/style)
- Use `dart format` for code formatting
- Maximum line length: 80 characters
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Always use trailing commas in multi-line parameter lists

## Naming Conventions
- Use `camelCase` for variables and functions
- Use `PascalCase` for classes and enums
- Use `lowercase_with_underscores` for file names
- Prefix private variables with underscore (`_`)
- Use meaningful, descriptive names

## Code Organization
- Group related code together
- Keep classes and functions focused and single-purpose
- Use appropriate access modifiers (public, private)
- Follow the SOLID principles
- Keep methods short and focused

## Comments and Documentation
- Use clear, concise comments
- Document all public APIs
- Use Dart documentation style for public members
- Keep comments up-to-date with code changes
- Remove commented-out code before committing

## Best Practices
- Use const constructors where possible
- Prefer final variables over var
- Use named parameters for clarity
- Implement proper null safety
- Follow the principle of least privilege
